            <ArticleTitle>Palm oil thorn-induced squamous cell carcinoma with underlying burns scar.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2012-006401</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2012006401</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Marjolin's ulcers are malignancies that arise from previously traumatised, chronically inflamed or scarred skin. We present a case with childhood burns, who had repeated irritation of his forearm skin with palm oil thorns that eventually led to malignant change.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
